#====================================================================
# Draft: Testing 3GPP AMR reference codecs - GP3 storage frame sizes
#        are exact (TOC+payload), decoder needs a few frames to
#        converge from reset, encoder CLI writes #!AMR magic
#        (libamrnb 11.0.0.0 consumer tests)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-13503-LIBAMRNB-AMR-CODEC-TEST-PROPERTIES
trigger_tool:           test|ctest|clang
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        decoded sine peak too low|mode \d: \d+ bytes|round-trip OK|#!AMR

severity:               1
category:               testing, limitation, codec, ohos, portability
match_keywords:         AMR, AMR-NB, MR475, MR122, GP3, IF2, ETSI, frame size, TOC, decoder convergence, cold start, sine peak, Encoder_Interface_Encode, Decoder_Interface_Decode, amrnb-encoder, AMR_MAGIC_NUMBER, test_package, ctest

title:                  AMR-NB consumer tests must (a) assert exact GP3 storage frame sizes per mode (13/14/16/18/20/21/27/32 bytes for MR475..MR122 = 1 TOC byte + RFC4867 payload), (b) run a multi-frame round-trip before amplitude assertions because the decoder needs 2-3 frames from reset state, and (c) smoke the encoder CLI by checking the #!AMR\n magic + frame count

root_cause:             The 3GPP TS 26.104 reference decoder starts from a reset state and its output amplitude ramps up over the first 2-3 frames; a single-frame encode/decode round-trip assertion like peak >= 4000 for an 8000-amplitude input sine fails even though the codec is fully functional (observed: single-frame peak far below threshold, 6-frame run converges to peak=4152 = 52% of input on the very first converged frame). Separately, the default (GP3) interface emits the storage format: 1 TOC/header byte plus the RFC 4867 payload per mode, so encoded byte counts are exact constants suitable for strict assertions; the amrnb-encoder/amrnb-decoder sample CLIs write/read streams prefixed with the 6-byte AMR_MAGIC_NUMBER "#!AMR\n".

affected_scope:         Consumer test_package tests for AMR-NB codecs (libamrnb wrapper over 3GPP TS 26.104; same interface shape as opencore-amr). Any test asserting decoded amplitude on the first frame, or eyeballing frame sizes.

verification_cmd:       conan create archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           exact-frame-sizes-plus-multiframe-convergence
rec_description:        Encode one 160-sample (20 ms @ 8 kHz) sine frame in each of the 8 modes and assert exact GP3 sizes {13,14,16,18,20,21,27,32}; for the round-trip encode/decode 6 identical MR122 frames and measure the output peak only from frame 3 onward (require >= 50% of input amplitude); for the CLI smoke write 320 samples of PCM, run amrnb-encoder MR122 in.pcm out.amr, assert out.amr starts with b"#!AMR\n" and has 6 + 2*32 bytes. DTX check: Encoder_Interface_init(1) on silence must yield a small SID frame (n>0, n<=32).
rec_command:            grep -n "expect_bytes" archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0/test_package/test.c
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/l/libamrnb/11.0.0.0/test_package/test.c (19 assertions) + test_package/conanfile.py CLI smoke

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      relaxed-range-assertions
fallback_description:   If exact sizes need to stay version-tolerant across codec releases, fall back to range checks (0 < n <= 32) - weaker but still proves a real encode; keep the multi-frame convergence requirement regardless, it is behavioral not cosmetic.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       assert amplitude on the first decoded frame|feed decoder homing frame and assert silence
forbid_1_reason:        First-frame amplitude assertions fail on a healthy codec (reset-state ramp), producing false CI reds; misusing the homing frame as a "silence proof" tests the reset contract, not the codec path.
forbid_1_consequence:   Flaky/false test failures unrelated to real regressions; wasted CI rounds (one full device round was burned on exactly this during libamrnb bring-up).

principles:             real-evidence-over-assumption, deterministic-tests, meaningful-assertions
